# Pairs with HandOffBound. A resumed hand-off completes while its marker is open,
# removing the marker instead of closing it by fence. No heads are recorded, so
# once L's marker state initialises it reads closed below the hand-off's stamped
# appends.
MODULE: HandOffBoundCompleteWithoutClose
TARGET: HandOffBound
CLASS: Invariant
SUMMARY: a resumed hand-off completes by dropping its open marker instead of closing it by fence
PERTURBS: LegacyComplete

--- FIND
    /\ resumed
    /\ ~hoOpen
    /\ ~fpend
    /\ hfly' = FALSE
    /\ fAdmit' = FALSE
    /\ UNCHANGED <<next, author, hoOpen, hoClosedAt,
--- REPLACE
    /\ resumed
    /\ ~fpend
    /\ hfly' = FALSE
    /\ fAdmit' = FALSE
\* MUTATION: the open marker is dropped, not closed by fence.
    /\ hoOpen' = FALSE
    /\ UNCHANGED <<next, author, hoClosedAt,
--- END
